WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:05.434
Does moringa live up to the hype?
Check out this video to find out.

00:00:05.434 --> 00:00:12.471
"The Benefits and Side Effects
of Moringa Leaf Powder"

00:00:13.683 --> 00:00:14.363
Moringa has been
called “the miracle tree,”

00:00:14.374 --> 00:00:15.680
Moringa (Moringa oleifera)
is a plant commonly known

00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:18.920
as the “miracle tree” due to
its purported healing powers

00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:21.160
across a spectrum of diseases.

00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:24.920
If “miracle” isn’t hyperbolic
enough for you, on the internet

00:00:24.920 --> 00:00:28.520
it’s also known as “God’s Gift to Man”.

00:00:28.520 --> 00:00:32.920
Is moringa a miracle or just a mirage?

00:00:32.920 --> 00:00:35.400
“The enthusiasm for the
health beneﬁts of [moringa] is

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:39.000
in dire contrast with the
scarcity of strong experimental

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:41.800
and clinical evidence
supporting [the claims].

00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:45.120
Fortunately, the chasm
is slowly being ﬁlled.”

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:47.960
There has been a surge in
scientiﬁc publications on moringa,

00:00:47.960 --> 00:00:49.560
and in the last ten years the number

00:00:49.560 --> 00:00:53.960
of articles is closer to a thousand.

00:00:53.960 --> 00:00:57.840
What got my attention was
the presence of glucosinolates,

00:00:57.840 --> 00:01:00.920
compounds that boost our
liver’s detoxifying enzymes.

00:01:00.920 --> 00:01:03.520
I thought they were only
found in cruciferous vegetables

00:01:03.520 --> 00:01:06.440
like cabbage, broccoli, kale,
collards, and cauliﬂower.

00:01:06.440 --> 00:01:11.080
But no, it turns out they’re
also found in the moringa family,

00:01:11.080 --> 00:01:13.800
with potency comparable to broccoli.

00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:17.400
That’s exciting, but why
not just eat broccoli,

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:20.600
rather than mail-ordering
some exotic moringa powder?

00:01:20.600 --> 00:01:23.880
Is there anything
special about moringa?

00:01:23.880 --> 00:01:29.040
It’s “been described as the
most nutritious tree yet discovered”.

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:32.720
How much is that saying,
though? Who eats trees?

00:01:32.720 --> 00:01:35.560
Supposedly moringa
“contains higher amounts of …

00:01:35.560 --> 00:01:37.600
nutrients than most
conventional … sources”:

00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:39.760
10 times the vitamin A of carrots,

00:01:39.760 --> 00:01:41.880
12 times the vitamin C of oranges,

00:01:41.880 --> 00:01:43.960
17 times more calcium than milk,

00:01:43.960 --> 00:01:46.920
15 times more potassium than bananas,

00:01:46.920 --> 00:01:48.760
25 times more iron than spinach,

00:01:48.760 --> 00:01:52.120
and 9 times more protein than yogurt.

00:01:52.120 --> 00:01:54.840
First of all, even if all this were true,

00:01:54.840 --> 00:01:58.600
this is for 100 grams
of dry moringa leaf.

00:01:58.600 --> 00:02:03.280
That’s like 14 tablespoons—
almost a whole cup of leaf powder.

00:02:03.280 --> 00:02:07.440
Researchers have had trouble
getting people to even eat 20 grams,

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:10.480
and so anything more would
likely “result in excessively

00:02:10.480 --> 00:02:14.800
unpleasant taste, due to the
bitterness of the leaves.”

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:17.840
And secondly, the nutritional
claims in these papers are

00:02:18.640 --> 00:02:23.600
"adapted from Fuglie," which
evidently is just some lay publication.

00:02:23.600 --> 00:02:27.200
If you go to the USDA nutrient
database, and enter a more

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:30.000
doable dose like the amount
you might get in a smoothie

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:33.920
(about one tablespoon for instance),
a serving of moringa powder

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:38.600
has as much vitamin A as
a quarter of one baby carrot,

00:02:38.600 --> 00:02:42.800
and as much vitamin C as
one one-hundredth of an orange.

00:02:42.800 --> 00:02:44.800
So, an orange has as much vitamin C

00:02:44.800 --> 00:02:48.320
as a hundred tablespoons of moringa.

00:02:48.320 --> 00:02:50.920
A serving of moringa powder
only has the calcium of

00:02:50.920 --> 00:02:54.560
half a cup of milk, the potassium
of not fifteen bananas,

00:02:54.560 --> 00:02:58.480
but a quarter of one banana, the
iron of a quarter cup of spinach,

00:02:58.480 --> 00:03:01.160
and the protein of a third
of a container of yogurt.

00:03:01.160 --> 00:03:04.400
So yeah, maybe nutritious,
but not off the charts

00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:06.880
and certainly not
what’s commonly touted.

00:03:06.880 --> 00:03:09.360
So again, why not eat broccoli?

00:03:09.360 --> 00:03:15.320
It’s got the A-C-Calcium-potassium-
iron-and-protein of broccoli!

00:03:15.320 --> 00:03:20.680
Moringa does seem to have
anticancer activity—in a petri dish—

00:03:20.680 --> 00:03:23.640
against cell lines of breast cancer,
lung cancer, skin cancer,

00:03:23.640 --> 00:03:27.080
and fibrosarcoma, while tending
to leave normal cells

00:03:27.080 --> 00:03:30.760
relatively alone, but there
haven’t been any clinical studies.

00:03:30.760 --> 00:03:33.680
What’s the point in finding
out that “[Moringa] … enhances

00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:36.120
[the] sexual performance
[of] stressed rats.”

00:03:36.800 --> 00:03:39.160
What are you supposed
to do with that?

00:03:39.160 --> 00:03:41.840
Studies like this one, though,
started to make things

00:03:41.840 --> 00:03:44.840
a little interesting.
Researchers were testing the effects

00:03:44.840 --> 00:03:48.080
of a tablespoon of moringa leaf
powder once a day for three months

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:52.080
on antioxidant status and saw
a drop in oxidative stress,

00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:56.280
as one might expect from
eating any healthy plant food.

00:03:56.280 --> 00:04:00.000
But they also saw a drop in
fasting blood sugars from

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:03.480
prediabetic levels over
100 to more normal levels.

00:04:03.480 --> 00:04:06.320
Now, that’s interesting.
Should we start recommending

00:04:06.320 --> 00:04:09.320
a daily tablespoon of moringa
powder to diabetics?

00:04:09.320 --> 00:04:12.880
Was it just a fluke?
Moringa and blood sugar control:

00:04:12.880 --> 00:04:18.800
A review of the current evidence... next.

00:04:18.800 --> 00:04:20.920
“Clearly, in spite of
the widely held “belief”

00:04:20.920 --> 00:04:23.760
in the health beneﬁts of
[moringa], the interest of

00:04:23.760 --> 00:04:26.920
the international biomedical community
in the medicinal potential

00:04:26.920 --> 00:04:31.440
of this plant has been rather
tepid”—“spectacularly hesitant

00:04:31.440 --> 00:04:34.960
[in fact,] in exploring its
nutritional and medicinal potential…

00:04:34.960 --> 00:04:37.800
other “superfoods” such as garlic
and green tea have enjoyed

00:04:37.800 --> 00:04:41.360
better reception,” but they also
have more scientific support.

00:04:41.360 --> 00:04:44.120
There are thousands of human
studies on garlic and more than

00:04:44.120 --> 00:04:48.920
ten thousand on green tea, but
only a few hundred on moringa.

00:04:48.920 --> 00:04:51.320
The most promising appears
to be on the effects

00:04:51.320 --> 00:04:54.000
of moringa on blood sugar control.

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:56.000
If you have people eat
about five cookies,

00:04:56.000 --> 00:04:58.440
this is the kind of
blood sugar spike you get.

00:04:58.440 --> 00:05:01.000
Add about two teaspoons
of moringa leaf powder

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:04.520
into the cookie batter, and even
with the same amount of sugar

00:05:04.520 --> 00:05:08.120
and carbs, the blood
sugar surge is dampened.

00:05:08.120 --> 00:05:09.760
Just having people
drink one or two cups

00:05:09.760 --> 00:05:12.720
of moringa leaf tea
before a sugar challenge

00:05:12.720 --> 00:05:15.240
“suppressed the elevation
in blood [sugar] in all cases

00:05:15.240 --> 00:05:18.920
compared to [those who
drank plain water instead].”

00:05:18.920 --> 00:05:21.360
Here’s the spike after
sugar with no moringa,

00:05:21.360 --> 00:05:23.760
and here’s the reaction to
the same amount of sugar

00:05:23.760 --> 00:05:27.640
30 minutes after
drinking moringa tea.

00:05:27.640 --> 00:05:30.240
No wonder moringa is
used in traditional

00:05:30.240 --> 00:05:33.720
medicine practice for diabetes.
But you don’t really know

00:05:33.720 --> 00:05:37.880
if it can help until
you put it to the test.

00:05:37.880 --> 00:05:40.560
Diabetics were given about
three-quarters of a teaspoon

00:05:40.560 --> 00:05:43.720
of moringa leaf powder every
day for 12 weeks and got

00:05:43.720 --> 00:05:46.600
significant improvements
in measures of inflammation

00:05:46.600 --> 00:05:49.360
as well as long-term
blood sugar control.

00:05:49.360 --> 00:05:53.080
But the reason they call it
a quasi-experimental study

00:05:53.080 --> 00:05:55.880
is because there was no control group.

00:05:55.880 --> 00:05:59.720
The researchers just took
measurements before and after,

00:05:59.720 --> 00:06:02.720
and we know that just being
in a dietary study can lead

00:06:02.720 --> 00:06:06.720
some people to consciously or
unconsciously eat more healthfully,

00:06:06.720 --> 00:06:10.560
so we don’t know what
effect the moringa itself had.

00:06:10.560 --> 00:06:12.960
Even in moringa studies
with a control group,

00:06:12.960 --> 00:06:16.440
it’s not clear if the subjects
were randomly allocated.

00:06:16.440 --> 00:06:18.840
And in this study, the
researchers didn’t specify

00:06:18.840 --> 00:06:21.720
how much moringa
people were even given.

00:06:21.720 --> 00:06:24.840
What does one tablet’s worth mean?

00:06:24.840 --> 00:06:27.160
No significant improvement
in this study;

00:06:27.160 --> 00:06:29.120
maybe they didn’t give enough?

00:06:29.120 --> 00:06:32.160
This study used a tablespoon
a day and not only saw

00:06:32.160 --> 00:06:34.480
a significant drop in
fasting blood sugars,

00:06:34.480 --> 00:06:37.800
but a significant drop
in LDL cholesterol as well.

00:06:37.800 --> 00:06:41.520
Two teaspoons a day didn’t
seem to help, so was it just

00:06:41.520 --> 00:06:44.440
that a whole tablespoon is needed?

00:06:44.440 --> 00:06:48.080
Apparently not, since finally,
a randomized placebo-controlled

00:06:48.080 --> 00:06:52.560
study using a tablespoon of
moringa a day failed to show

00:06:52.560 --> 00:06:58.160
any benefit on blood sugar
control in type 2 diabetics.

00:06:58.160 --> 00:07:00.680
So, we’re left with a few
studies showing potential

00:07:00.680 --> 00:07:03.880
but most failing to show benefit.

00:07:03.880 --> 00:07:07.840
Why not just give moringa
a try to see for yourself?

00:07:07.840 --> 00:07:10.320
That’s a legitimate course
of action in the face of

00:07:10.320 --> 00:07:13.600
conflicting data when we’re
talking about safe, simple,

00:07:13.600 --> 00:07:15.280
side effect free solutions.

00:07:15.280 --> 00:07:17.920
But is moringa safe?

00:07:17.920 --> 00:07:21.520
Probably not during pregnancy,
as about 80 percent

00:07:21.520 --> 00:07:24.920
of “women folk” in some
areas of the world use it

00:07:24.920 --> 00:07:28.800
to abort pregnancies, and its
effectiveness for that purpose

00:07:28.800 --> 00:07:31.960
has been confirmed, at least in rats;

00:07:31.960 --> 00:07:34.960
though breastfeeding women
may get about a half cup

00:07:34.960 --> 00:07:37.880
boost in milk production
based on “six randomized,

00:07:37.880 --> 00:07:41.320
placebo-controlled,
blinded, clinical trials”.

00:07:41.320 --> 00:07:43.280
Just because moringa
has “long been used

00:07:43.280 --> 00:07:46.800
in [folk medicine traditions]”
in no way proves

00:07:46.800 --> 00:07:49.000
that the plant is safe to consume.

00:07:49.000 --> 00:07:52.840
Lots of horribly toxic stuff,
like mercury and lead

00:07:52.840 --> 00:07:54.720
for instance, have
been used in traditional

00:07:54.720 --> 00:07:57.320
medical systems the world over.

00:07:57.320 --> 00:08:00.160
But hey, at least “no major
harmful effects of [moringa] …

00:08:00.160 --> 00:08:03.480
have been reported by
the scientiﬁc community”,

00:08:03.480 --> 00:08:06.040
or more accurately, “no adverse
effects were reported

00:08:06.040 --> 00:08:09.600
in any of the human studies that
[had] been conducted to date.”

00:08:09.600 --> 00:08:16.920
In other words, no harmful effects
had been reported... until now.

00:08:16.920 --> 00:08:21.880
“Stevens-Johnson syndrome …
following [moringa leaf] consumption”:

00:08:21.880 --> 00:08:26.360
Stevens-Johnson syndrome is
probably the most dreaded drug

00:08:26.360 --> 00:08:30.720
side effect, a rare but
potentially fatal condition

00:08:30.720 --> 00:08:34.040
characterized by
“epidermal detachment.”

00:08:34.040 --> 00:08:39.080
In other words, it can
make your skin fall off.

00:08:39.080 --> 00:08:43.040
Fourteen hours after consuming
moringa, a guy broke out.

00:08:43.040 --> 00:08:45.360
The same thing had happened
three months earlier,

00:08:45.360 --> 00:08:48.440
the last time he had eaten
moringa, causing him to suffer

00:08:48.440 --> 00:08:51.040
“extensive lesions with
blister formation

00:08:51.040 --> 00:08:55.320
over [his] face, mouth, chest,
abdomen, and genitalia.”

00:08:55.320 --> 00:08:57.920
“This case report
suggests that consumption

00:08:57.920 --> 00:09:01.000
of Moringa leaf is better
avoided by individuals

00:09:01.000 --> 00:09:04.000
who are at risk of
developing [Stevens-Johnson].”

00:09:04.000 --> 00:09:07.440
Although it can happen to
anyone, HIV is a risk factor.

00:09:07.440 --> 00:09:10.640
My take on moringa is that
the evidence of benefit

00:09:10.640 --> 00:09:13.560
wasn’t compelling enough
to justify shopping online

00:09:13.560 --> 00:09:16.920
for something special when
you can get healthy vegetables

00:09:16.920 --> 00:09:20.280
in your local market like
broccoli which has yet

00:09:20.280 --> 00:09:24.865
to be implicated in
any genital blistering.

